      "description": "What if Wu-Tang Clan never came together on Staten Island—and Enter the Wu-Tang (36 Chambers) never existed? Hip Hop What If rewinds the real early-1990s Wu-Tang story, then branches into an alternate timeline where RZA’s plan never fully unites the crew. Method Man, Ghostface Killah, Raekwon, GZA, Ol’ Dirty Bastard and the rest still have talent—but without one central movement, the solo careers, business blueprint, New York rap landscape and worldwide Wu mythology all change. This is alternate-history commentary. The historical setup is factual; events after the branch point are hypothetical.",
